1. Enable Privileged Mode
Switch> enable
Switch#

2. Enter Global Configuration Mode
Switch# configure terminal
Switch(config)#

3. Disable DNS Lookup
Prevents the switch from trying to resolve mistyped commands as hostnames.
Switch(config)# no ip domain lookup

4. Set Hostname
Switch(config)# hostname SW-ACCESS-01
SW-ACCESS-01(config)#

5. Set Time Zone and Time
For Bangladesh:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# clock timezone BDT 6 0
Set the clock manually if necessary:
SW-ACCESS-01# clock set 09:20:00 20 September 2026
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show clock
Once NTP is working, NTP should be the preferred time source.

6. Configure NTP Server
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# ntp server 172.16.32.11
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show ntp status
SW-ACCESS-01# show ntp associations
If the NTP server is unreachable, check:
SW-ACCESS-01# ping 172.16.32.11

7. Configure Syslog Server
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# logging host 172.30.101.20
Set an appropriate logging level:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# logging trap warnings
Set timestamps:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# service timestamps log datetime msec
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show logging

8. Configure SNMP
For a modern deployment, SNMPv3 is preferable.
SNMPv3 example
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# snmp-server view NMSVIEW iso included
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# snmp-server group NMSGROUP v3 priv read NMSVIEW
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# snmp-server user NMSUSER NMSGROUP v3 auth sha AuthPassword123 priv aes 128 PrivPassword123
Configure your NMS/SNMP server:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# snmp-server host 172.30.101.30 version 3 priv NMSUSER
Set the device location/contact:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# snmp-server location Main Office
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# snmp-server contact Network-Admin
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show snmp
SW-ACCESS-01# show snmp user

9. Configure CDP and LLDP
CDP
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# cdp run
LLDP
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# lldp run
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show cdp neighbors
SW-ACCESS-01# show lldp neighbors

10. Configure Enable Secret
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# enable secret StrongEnablePassword
enable secret is preferred over the older enable password.

11. Create Local User with Full Privilege
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# username admin privilege 15 secret StrongAdminPassword
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show running-config | include username
You should see an encrypted/hashed secret rather than the plain password.

12. Verify Local User
SW-ACCESS-01# show running-config | include username

13. Configure Console with Logging Synchronous
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# line console 0
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# login local
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# logging synchronous
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# exec-timeout 10 0
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# exit
This prevents system messages from disrupting your command line.

14. Enable Telnet
Telnet is insecure because credentials are transmitted without encryption. If it is required for legacy management, configure it separately from SSH.
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# line vty 0 4
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# login local
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# transport input telnet
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# logging synchronous
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# exec-timeout 10 0
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# exit
If your switch has VTY lines 5-15, configure them too:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# line vty 5 15
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# login local
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# transport input telnet
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# logging synchronous
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# exec-timeout 10 0
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# exit

15. Enable SSH
First configure the domain name:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# ip domain name edison-bd.com
Generate RSA keys:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# crypto key generate rsa modulus 2048
Set SSH version 2:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# ip ssh version 2
Configure VTY for SSH.
If you want SSH + Telnet:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# line vty 0 4
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# login local
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# transport input ssh telnet
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# logging synchronous
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# exit
If you want SSH only, which is preferable:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# line vty 0 4
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# login local
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# transport input ssh
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# logging synchronous
SW-ACCESS-01(config-line)# exit
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show ip ssh

16. Configure VLANs
Create management VLAN:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# vlan 101
SW-ACCESS-01(config-vlan)# name MANAGEMENT
SW-ACCESS-01(config-vlan)# exit
Create camera VLAN:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# vlan 216
SW-ACCESS-01(config-vlan)# name CAMERA
SW-ACCESS-01(config-vlan)# exit
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show vlan brief

17. Configure Uplink
Assume Gi1/0/24 is the uplink.
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface GigabitEthernet1/0/24
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# description ### UPLINK-TO-DISTRIBUTION ###
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# switchport mode trunk
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 101,216
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# no shutdown
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# exit
On platforms that support it, you can explicitly remove VLAN 1:
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 101,216
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show interfaces trunk

18. Set Remote IP in Management VLAN and Gateway
Create the SVI:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface vlan 101
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# description ### MANAGEMENT ###
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# ip address 172.30.101.10 255.255.255.0
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# no shutdown
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# exit
For a Layer-2 switch, configure the default gateway:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# ip default-gateway 172.30.101.1
This is the normal approach for an L2 access switch.
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show ip interface brief
SW-ACCESS-01# ping 172.30.101.1

19. Configure Downlinks
For camera ports, for example Gi1/0/1-23:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface range GigabitEthernet1/0/1 - 23
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# description ### CAMERA ###
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# switchport mode access
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# switchport access vlan 216
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# spanning-tree portfast
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# spanning-tree bpduguard enable
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# no shutdown
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# exit
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show vlan brief
SW-ACCESS-01# show interfaces status

20. Configure Spanning Tree
For a typical access switch:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# spanning-tree mode rapid-pvst
Check:
SW-ACCESS-01# show spanning-tree
If your organization uses MST instead, don't enable Rapid-PVST blindly; the entire STP design should be consistent.

21. PortFast + BPDU Guard
For end-device ports:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface range GigabitEthernet1/0/1 - 23
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# spanning-tree portfast
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# spanning-tree bpduguard enable
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# exit
Alternatively, globally:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# spanning-tree portfast default
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# spanning-tree portfast bpduguard default
Do not apply PortFast to your uplink/trunk ports.

22. Configure DHCP Snooping
Enable DHCP Snooping:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# ip dhcp snooping
Enable it for the VLAN:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# ip dhcp snooping vlan 101,216
Trust the uplink toward the legitimate DHCP server:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface GigabitEthernet1/0/24
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# ip dhcp snooping trust
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# exit
Do not trust normal end-device ports.
Verify:
SW-ACCESS-01# show ip dhcp snooping
SW-ACCESS-01# show ip dhcp snooping binding

23. Configure Port Descriptions
Example:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface Gi1/0/1
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# description ### CAMERA-01 ###
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# exit

SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface Gi1/0/2
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# description ### CAMERA-02 ###
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# exit
For the uplink:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface Gi1/0/24
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# description ### UPLINK-TO-DIST-SW ###
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if)# exit
Good descriptions make troubleshooting much easier.

24. Disable Unused Ports and Services
Suppose ports Gi1/0/20-23 are unused:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface range Gi1/0/20 - 23
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# description ### UNUSED ###
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# shutdown
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# exit
You can also disable unnecessary services, depending on your environment.
For example, if CDP is not required on an end-user port:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# interface range Gi1/0/1 - 23
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# no cdp enable
SW-ACCESS-01(config-if-range)# exit
However, don't disable CDP/LLDP globally if you use them for network topology discovery.

25. Verify Gateway, Uplink and Remote Connectivity
Check interfaces
SW-ACCESS-01# show ip interface brief
Check VLANs
SW-ACCESS-01# show vlan brief
Check trunk
SW-ACCESS-01# show interfaces trunk
Check gateway
SW-ACCESS-01# ping 172.30.101.1
Check remote management/NMS
SW-ACCESS-01# ping 172.30.101.20
SW-ACCESS-01# ping 172.30.101.30
Check uplink neighbor
SW-ACCESS-01# show cdp neighbors detail
Check LLDP
SW-ACCESS-01# show lldp neighbors detail
Check STP
SW-ACCESS-01# show spanning-tree

26. Save Configuration
First check:
SW-ACCESS-01# show running-config
Then save:
SW-ACCESS-01# copy running-config startup-config
Press Enter when asked for the destination filename.
You can also use:
SW-ACCESS-01# write memory

27. Check Remote Login
27. Check Configuration
Useful final checks:
show running-config
show startup-config
show vlan brief
show interfaces status
show interfaces trunk
show ip interface brief
show spanning-tree
show ip dhcp snooping
show logging
show ntp status
show cdp neighbors
show lldp neighbors
show ip ssh
show users

28. Configure MOTD
I would actually put this near the beginning of the configuration, but following your requested order:
SW-ACCESS-01(config)# banner motd #
************************************************************
* WARNING: Authorized Access Only                          *
* This device is monitored and all activities are logged. *
************************************************************
#
When connecting:
************************************************************
* WARNING: Authorized Access Only                          *
* This device is monitored and all activities are logged. *
************************************************************

